{"kind": "result", "at": "2026-11-02T18:24:03.784377+00:00", "task": "app_migration", "attempt": 1, "trial_id": "t-f5a84d967d6d42ce8b4d7ae340d910a1", "verdict": "INFRA_ERROR", "reason": "behavioral_job:eso_not_synced", "s": 417.7, "view": {"trial_id": "t-f5a84d967d6d42ce8b4d7ae340d910a1", "plan_id": "778b074a-a07a-4362-8987-0481e4aa4e67", "rehearsal_id": "91c9f649-6a84-40da-98e5-2ac4f636d1b4", "attempt": 1, "task": "app-migration", "role": "app_migration", "phase": "done", "verdict": "INFRA_ERROR", "reason": "behavioral_job:eso_not_synced", "artifact": {"plan_id": "p-778b074a-a07a-4362-8987-0481e4aa4e67", "trial_id": "t-f5a84d967d6d42ce8b4d7ae340d910a1", "attempt": 1, "rationale": "Removed the direct AWS Secrets Manager dependency (inv:3ccbf876f57f08e8 boto3.client('secretsmanager') at secrets.py:41, inv:9de663601b600ca9 get_secret_value at secrets.py:48) together with its selection branch. The DB password is now read only from the landing-zone mounted file DB_PASSWORD_FILE (ESO-synced K8s Secret bravo-demo-db from OpenBao, mounted at /var/run/bravo/db/password per destination_profile). config.load() no longer requires DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE and no longer reads DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ID/_KEY/_REGION/_ENDPOINT_URL or AWS_REGION; it requires DB_DSN and DB_PASSWORD_FILE only, so the app starts with exactly what the destination provides and makes no cloud API call. Pre-fix code fails under the same conditions (DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE is required there). DbSettings keeps password_source as the constant 'env-file' so app.py's startup log and secrets.py log stay unchanged; DSN validation, attachments, write-block switch and logging are unchanged. The S3 findings (inv:baa6de5a5e72c850, inv:4b2a570efa066af8) already use the config-driven S3_ENDPOINT_URL, so no change was needed. inv:a5ccbeca75df0ace (DSN) is no_change. Chart findings (inv:ecedbaf5b23990db, inv:c6b9dab5de3d8a70) are deployment files and out of scope. Note: the existing ConfigError text 'use DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE' on the DSN-password check was deliberately left unchanged. The platform view redacts the line next to it, and editing the message would have put that redacted text into the diff context and made the patch fail to apply. A follow-up can change the message to say DB_PASSWORD_FILE. No dependencies, tests, CI or deployment files changed (pyproject still lists boto3, which S3 uses). compile passes; the diff is the verbatim make_diff output.", "risk": "low", "evidence_refs": ["inv:3ccbf876f57f08e8", "inv:9de663601b600ca9", "inv:baa6de5a5e72c850", "inv:4b2a570efa066af8", "inv:a5ccbeca75df0ace", "inv:c6b9dab5de3d8a70"], "role": "app_migration", "step": "fix", "diff": "diff -ruN src/src/bravo_demo/config.py app/src/bravo_demo/config.py\n--- src/src/bravo_demo/config.py\t1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000\n+++ app/src/bravo_demo/config.py\t2026-11-02 18:19:07.457184092 +0000\n@@ -70,12 +70,8 @@\n class DbSettings:\n     # libpq DSN without the password, e.g. \"host=pgbouncer port=6432 dbname=chat user=app_writer\".\n     dsn: str\n-    password_source: str  # aws-secrets-manager | env-file\n-    password_file: str | None\n-    secret_id: str | None\n-    secret_key: str | None  # JSON key inside the secret; None = the secret string is the password\n-    secrets_region: str | None\n-    secrets_endpoint_url: str | None\n+    password_source: str  # always env-file: the landing zone mounts the password as a file\n+    password_file: str\n     pool_min: int\n     pool_max: int\n     statement_timeout_ms: int  # per write transaction (SET LOCAL), §8.10 max 200 ms\n@@ -147,18 +143,11 @@\n     keys, an on-prem S3-compatible store): there is no per-cloud code path.\"\"\"\n     env = dict(os.environ) if env is None else env\n \n-    source = _req(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE\")\n-    if source not in (\"aws-secrets-manager\", \"env-file\"):\n-        raise ConfigError(\"DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE must be aws-secrets-manager or env-file\")\n     statement_timeout_ms = _int(env, \"DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS\", 200, 10, 200)\n     db = DbSettings(\n         dsn=_req(env, \"DB_DSN\"),\n-        password_source=source,\n-        password_file=_req(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_FILE\") if source == \"env-file\" else None,\n-        secret_id=_req(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ID\") if source == \"aws-secrets-manager\" else None,\n-        secret_key=_opt(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_KEY\"),\n-        secrets_region=_opt(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_REGION\") or _opt(env, \"AWS_REGION\"),\n-        secrets_endpoint_url=_opt(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ENDPOINT_URL\"),\n+        password_source=\"env-file\",  # noqa: S106 - a mode name, not a secret\n+        password_file=_req(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_FILE\"),\n         pool_min=_int(env, \"DB_POOL_MIN\", 1, 0, 50),\n         pool_max=_int(env, \"DB_POOL_MAX\", 8, 1, 100),\n         statement_timeout_ms=statement_timeout_ms,\ndiff -ruN src/src/bravo_demo/secrets.py app/src/bravo_demo/secrets.py\n--- src/src/bravo_demo/secrets.py\t1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000\n+++ app/src/bravo_demo/secrets.py\t2026-11-02 18:18:22.774086507 +0000\n@@ -1,14 +1,12 @@\n-\"\"\"Database password sources (§8.10).\n+\"\"\"Database password source (§8.10).\n \n-``aws-secrets-manager`` calls the AWS Secrets Manager API directly with the SDK at startup.\n-This direct cloud dependency is intentional: it is the \"code fix\" material of scenario S2.\n-``env-file`` reads a mounted file (Kubernetes Secret, Docker secret); this is the mode the\n-fix switches to, so the app no longer calls a cloud API.\n+The password is read only from a mounted file (``DB_PASSWORD_FILE``): on the landing zone a\n+Kubernetes Secret synced by External Secrets from the platform OpenBao. The app calls no\n+cloud API and needs no cloud credentials.\n \"\"\"\n \n from __future__ import annotations\n \n-import json\n import logging\n from pathlib import Path\n \n@@ -31,51 +29,9 @@\n     return value\n \n \n-def _from_secrets_manager(settings: DbSettings) -> str:\n-    import boto3  # imported here: the env-file mode must not need AWS at all\n-    from botocore.config import Config\n-    from botocore.exceptions import BotoCoreError, ClientError\n-\n-    if not settings.secret_id:\n-        raise ConfigError(\"DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ID is required\")\n-    client = boto3.client(\n-        \"secretsmanager\",\n-        region_name=settings.secrets_region,\n-        endpoint_url=settings.secrets_endpoint_url,\n-        config=Config(connect_timeout=3, read_timeout=5, retries={\"max_attempts\": 3, \"mode\": \"standard\"}),\n-    )\n-    try:\n-        resp = client.get_secret_value(SecretId=settings.secret_id)\n-    except ClientError as exc:\n-        code = exc.response.get(\"Error\", {}).get(\"Code\", \"Unknown\")\n-        raise SecretError(f\"Secrets Manager GetSecretValue failed: {code}\") from exc\n-    except BotoCoreError as exc:\n-        raise SecretError(f\"Secrets Manager call failed: {type(exc).__name__}\") from exc\n-    raw = resp.get(\"SecretString\")\n-    if raw is None:\n-        raise SecretError(\"secret has no SecretString\")\n-    if settings.secret_key:\n-        try:\n-            doc = json.loads(raw)\n-        except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n-            raise SecretError(\"secret is not JSON but DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_KEY is set\") from exc\n-        value = doc.get(settings.secret_key) if isinstance(doc, dict) else None\n-        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value:\n-            raise SecretError(\"secret JSON has no string value for DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_KEY\")\n-        return value\n-    if not raw:\n-        raise SecretError(\"secret string is empty\")\n-    return raw\n-\n-\n def db_password(settings: DbSettings) -> str:\n-    if settings.password_source == \"env-file\":  # noqa: S105 - a mode name, not a secret\n-        if not settings.password_file:\n-            raise ConfigError(\"DB_PASSWORD_FILE is required\")\n-        value = _from_file(settings.password_file)\n-    elif settings.password_source == \"aws-secrets-manager\":  # noqa: S105 - a mode name\n-        value = _from_secrets_manager(settings)\n-    else:  # config.load() rejects anything else\n-        raise ConfigError(\"unknown DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE\")\n+    if not settings.password_file:\n+        raise ConfigError(\"DB_PASSWORD_FILE is required\")\n+    value = _from_file(settings.password_file)\n     log.info(\"database password loaded\", extra={\"source\": settings.password_source})\n     return value\n", "files": ["src/bravo_demo/secrets.py", "src/bravo_demo/config.py"], "sdk_calls_replaced": [{"file": "src/bravo_demo/secrets.py", "line": 41, "before_api": "boto3.client('secretsmanager')", "after": "removed; no cloud client is created"}, {"file": "src/bravo_demo/secrets.py", "line": 48, "before_api": "secretsmanager.GetSecretValue", "after": "read the mounted file at DB_PASSWORD_FILE (_from_file)"}], "config_changes": [{"key": "DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE", "before": "required: aws-secrets-manager | env-file", "after": "removed (password always read from DB_PASSWORD_FILE)"}, {"key": "DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ID", "before": "required when DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE=aws-secrets-manager", "after": "removed"}, {"key": "DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_KEY", "before": "optional JSON key inside the Secrets Manager secret", "after": "removed"}, {"key": "DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_REGION", "before": "optional Secrets Manager region (fallback AWS_REGION)", "after": "removed"}, {"key": "DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ENDPOINT_URL", "before": "optional Secrets Manager endpoint", "after": "removed"}, {"key": "DB_PASSWORD_FILE", "before": "required only when DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE=env-file", "after": "always required; landing-zone mount /var/run/bravo/db/password (Secret bravo-demo-db, key password)"}]}, "artifact_digest": "sha256:935d8bc08800877bff7bbde7f5b53b40cf86c95ff3e16bf4ad41746fa5c43059", "verifier": {"run_id": "verify-778b074a-app-1/verify-runner-t-f5a84d967d", "pod_uid": "17c48128-f8e9-4ac1-8192-2b569d42c37b", "image_digest": "sha256:6dd8b6dab6b3adc7812bab69eca5dbdc1a5cc690ad28306d234f